---
/**
 * The app's Home screen, built in HTML and CSS instead of a screenshot, in
 * its iPhone frame (Paper P3 Web hero A9Q-0 / B7Z-0, app Home 14O7-0): status
 * bar, header (eye, mark, bell with 4, avatar), "October · day 10 of 31",
 * AED 10,288.34 spent, the month bar (spent, today's tick, the hatched savings
 * set aside at the end), the verdict, the Needs / Wants / Savings tiles, "Your
 * widgets" (Budget pace, Next bill, Net worth) and the tab bar. Every glyph is
 * text or vector, so it is sharp at any zoom.
 *
 * 418 x 900 at 1x; the page scales the whole frame. Figures never wrap
 * (nowrap) and the big one is sized in container units, so it shrinks with
 * the screen rather than reflowing.
 *
 * Motion (Paper 13 · Dynamic layer, C83-0): the first time it is shown, the
 * figure counts up with the bar (900 ms, ease-in-out), the today tick drops
 * in, the verdict lands, the tiles and widgets rise one after another and the
 * widget bars and the net-worth line draw. `play` picks when that happens:
 * "hero" once per tab session (html.hero-seen, like the rest of the hero),
 * "load" once per full page load (not after a client-side navigation,
 * html.routed). Then a slow idle float, paused while off screen. With reduced
 * motion it is simply shown in its final state.
 *
 * The entrance is pure CSS: the keyframe names are custom properties that
 * exist only while it should play, so without them every `animation` is
 * invalid and the screen is drawn final. A few lines of script count the
 * figure and pause the idle float off screen (any [data-alive] ancestor).
 *
 * The frame is aria-hidden; `label` is read instead (omit it where the whole
 * stage is decorative, as on /i).
 */
interface Props {
  play: 'hero' | 'load';
  label?: string;
  class?: string;
}
const { play, label, class: extra } = Astro.props;
const uid = `hp-${play}`;
---

<div class:list={['hp', `hp--${play}`, extra]}>
  {label && <p class="sr-only">{label}</p>}
  <div class="hp__device" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="hp__screen">
      <div class="hp__wash"></div>

      <div class="hp__status">
